# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
dev-dist
*.local

# Env — Supabase keys land here from Session 1 on. Never commit these.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Supabase CLI local state — created by `supabase link` (project ref,
# pooler/db connection metadata) and `supabase db pull`/branching.
# Local-machine state, not something the repo should carry, and
# potentially sensitive (connection details) depending on CLI version.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
.supabase/

# Auto-generated by the TanStack Router plugin on every `vite dev` /
# `vite build` — never hand-edited, never committed.
src/routeTree.gen.ts
.tanstack/

# src/types/database.generated.ts is NOT ignored, unlike the above: it
# only updates via an explicit, infrequent `pnpm db:types` run against a
# live Supabase instance, not automatically on every dev/build. It's
# committed so `pnpm typecheck`/`pnpm build` work for anyone cloning the
# repo without running codegen first — still never hand-edited once real
# generated output exists (CLAUDE.md §3).

# Claude Code local runtime state (session locks, PIDs) — machine- and
# session-specific, never shared config. .claude/settings.json (the
# tracked permission allowlist) is unaffected by this pattern.
.claude/*.lock

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
